  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6dbb-9ca4-08b2-c4d2" name="English (Shieldwall) - List Notes" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false">
      <description>ENGLISH ARMY LISTS (Shieldwall, pp.17-25): Wessex, Mercia, Northumbria, Anglia and Kent &amp; the Home Counties. Percentages are by points. Special rules pp.20-23.
Huscarls: the army may split its single unit of Huscarls and combine them with units of Ceorls (no more than 25% Huscarls or 50% Thegns in the combined unit; Thegns and Huscarls may not be mixed) - see the Combined Units rule; combined units are formed on the table, not in the roster.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Wessex]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  Wessex (p.20). Characters up to 33% (25% if the army includes Huscarls); the army may be led by a Cyning or an Eorl. Huscarls, Thegns or Ceorls at least 50%; Geburs and Dogs of War (Vikings, Freebooters, Stipendarii) up to 25%; no more than half of the Gebur models may be bow-armed. Veterans: Thegns may, once per battle, re-roll all their hit dice for close combat or shooting (the whole roll must be re-rolled and abided by). The army may not have more units of mounted Thegns than of dismounted Thegns.
[Mercia]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Mercia (pp.20-21). Characters up to 33% (25% if the army includes Huscarls); led by a Cyning or an Eorl. Huscarls, Thegns or Ceorls at least 50%; Geburs and Dogs of War (Vikings, Freebooters, Bradwr) up to 33%. Any unit of Thegns may be designated as light infantry; such a unit cannot combine with Ceorls.
[Northumbria]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: up to 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Northumbria (p.21). Characters up to 33% (25% if the army includes Huscarls); led by a Cyning or an Eorl. Huscarls or Thegns up to 50% (Ceorls are not available); Geburs and Dogs of War (Gasraidh, Vikings, Gestir, Freebooters) up to 33%; no more than half of the Gebur models may be bow-armed. Thegns and Huscarls may exchange thrusting spears for throwing spears at no additional cost. Spear and shield-armed Gebur may combine with Thegns and Huscarls.
[Anglia]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: up to 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Anglia (p.21). Characters up to 33% (25% if the army includes Huscarls); the army may not be led by a Cyning. Huscarls or Thegns up to 50% (Ceorls are not available); Geburs and Dogs of War (Vikings, Gestir, Freebooters) up to 33%; no more than half of the Gebur models may be bow-armed. If the King is killed, all Ealdormen become subject to Hatred; any unit that includes Ealdormen also becomes subject to hatred of the enemy. Spear and shield-armed Gebur may combine with Thegns and Huscarls.
[Kent &amp; the Home Counties]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 33%
  Kent &amp; the Home Counties (p.21). Characters up to 33% (25% if the army includes Huscarls); led by a Cyning or an Eorl. Huscarls, Thegns or Ceorls at least 50%; Geburs and Dogs of War (Vikings, Freebooters, Serjeants) up to 33%; no more than half of the Gebur models may be bow-armed. Any Thegns or Ceorls may exchange thrusting spears for throwing spears at no additional cost.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
